00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:06.060
Episode Nineteen: 
Cry Baby, Hot-head

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.260
You were on a mission, just you and Kouta.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.580
It felt like being on a trip, didn't it?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.270
Did you make sure to do your work?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.810
Oh, yeah, after we saw you and Infi off...

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.530
...Pierre asked Yayoi out to a movie.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.660
And kaboom, she sunk him completely.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.640
And it looks like he went with Dai-chan...

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.560
...but naturally, the movie was a romance.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.770
It was two boys going to see "Passionate Andalusia".

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.240
Hey, did something happen during the mission?

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.510
Nothing.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:46.700
That's a lie.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:47.740
It's true.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.070
Even though you didn't eat a single bite of your dinner?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.690
I was... full...

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.060
But you're eating compeito, aren't you?

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.570
Something happened, right? Tell me.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.870
You wouldn't understand, Arisa.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.280
You don't know that until you tell me about it, right?

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.450
I do know.
Do you?

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:07.900
I don't.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.600
Which is it?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.360
Do whatever you want!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.620
And then, all of the sudden, she just started to cry.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.270
She just kept crying the whole time we were on the mission.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.090
I was confused.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.060
Anything come to mind?

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.890
Nothing. I don't understand at all.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.400
Girls are complex.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.470
We're not going to stand for letting boys understand us.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.780
Boys are complex, too.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.030
I wonder.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.990
Didn't you say so recently?

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.140
That's what's so simple about you.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.490
What do you mean by that?

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.420
And I thought that Shima-chan would understand, too.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.380
And then, the heroine, she says, "I can't believe this, I hate you!"

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.900
Why? I mean, didn't they kiss?

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.160
Yeah. But she said she hates him.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.840
Maybe the subtitles were wrong?

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.310
This wasn't an old movie. There wouldn't be any subtitles.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.070
Well then, why?

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.590
Well, that is...

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.570
It's a good thing you didn't go with Milady, isn't it?

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:12.760
Why's that?

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.920
Well, after the movie, if your impressions were different...

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.860
...she'd be disillusioned, wouldn't she?

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:17.960
Really?!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.520
If someone said they liked the heroine I hated...

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.850
...man, that would be the worst.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:25.390
What?

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.830
Um... the movie we saw recently... was it fun to watch?

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:29.820
Wha...?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.710
Oh, ho... so the two of you went to see a movie?

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.010
What? Which movie?
What...?

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.500
Perverted movies aren't allowed!
What...?

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.680
I hate you!

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.040
What?! So it really wasn't fun, then?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.270
You've already finished shipping off the graduation name register?

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.590
You're getting finished faster than we did when we did this.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.980
It's thanks to the advice all of you have given us.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.890
That's not it. This year's preparatory students are excellent.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:57.920
Wow!

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.770
It's the Stellvia! 
It's huge!

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.060
The cake gets put onto this papier-mâché model.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.230
It's like a wedding cake.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.330
I heard that a giant cake was going to be at the graduation ceremony, but...

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.160
So it's what's always used...

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.860
Surprised, weren't you?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.830
What? Yes...

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.460
Oh, jeez... I was so surprised.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.280
Even you, upperclassman Kent?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.600
This is a school tradition.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.640
You guys be sure to do this next year, okay?

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:32.990
Of course!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.890
Let's use a light or something, too, when we do this.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.250
Before you do that...

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.160
...you need to set up the lights for this year's party, right?

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.390
Er... Right.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.970
Did something happen?

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:50.670
What?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.510
You were forcing yourself to smile earlier.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.250
So you knew.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.040
What's wrong?

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.970
I was trying to go along with everyone and pretend to be surprised.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:02.670
What?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.760
Because I knew about the surprise from before.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.170
I was in charge of the graduation ceremony two years ago, too.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.920
No, that's not it. I just missed my timing to smile.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.890
Really, that's all it was.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.830
No one here had been in a war for 200 years.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.810
Even so, that doesn't mean it was all right to lose.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.050
And in the end, we still don't know who the enemy is...

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.450
You successfully pulled off an evacuation battle.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.420
It's not a loss at all.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.060
And the enemy's true identity...

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.530
...will be revealed using the data that Infi brought back.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.360
Otoyama's senses were beyond anything we imagined, after all.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.700
And even if Katase's aren't as strong as Otoyama's...

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.520
...it can be said that she's outstanding and excellent.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.730
I'm telling you, that is what's so pathetic.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.570
To go so far as to bring the students into this...

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.340
And I wasn't able to do anything myself.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.190
You're very cool today, Jinrai.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.740
R-Really?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.060
It's the first time I've thought it might be okay to fall for you.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.390
Hey now, so what did you feel up until now?

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.940
Hey, want to go drinking tonight?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.970
But Leila said she had something to do tonight.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.210
It's all right.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.760
Now and then the two of us should go... by ourselves.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.680
R-Right!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.980
I can't do it as skillfully as you can. I'm not a genius.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.300
What did you want to talk about?

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.820
Did something happen between you and Shipon?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.000
No...

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:53.190
Really?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:54.810
Nothing at all.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.340
That's why I'm mad.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:57.000
What?

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.950
But thanks for being worried.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:05.220
It's unusual for you to worry like this, Akira.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.540
This is usually Yayoi's job.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.980
This might be my fault.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:11.640
Huh?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.440
Before she went on the mission...

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.480
I told her that I wasn't a genius like her.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.410
That it was tough to be around her...

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.550
Why did you say something like that?

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:22.680
I just did...

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.360
You don't just say things like that!

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.190
What were you planning to do if Shipon had an accident...

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.410
...because of what you said?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:29.360
I'm sorry...

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.550
Sorry doesn't cut it!

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.270
You know how hard she's trying, too, Akira!

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.960
It's not like she became good just by doing nothing!

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.030
I know...

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.800
But I was frustrated...

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:44.310
Shipon is doing her best. So am I.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.620
But our results are different...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.550
Shipon joined the adults on their mission...

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:53.850
...and I'm floating around the middle of the preparatory student rankings.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.890
That's just your jealousy, isn't it?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:58.790
That's so selfish...

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.450
...making Shipon feel bad by saying that...

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:02.630
And why are you telling me, anyways?

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:04.610
The right thing to do is to tell Shipon!

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.820
It's not fair for you to run away from such an important thing, Akira!

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.390
You wouldn't understand, Arisa!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.290
What do you mean?

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.540
I'm saying that you, who ran off to a place...

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.740
...where you aren't compared to Shipon, wouldn't understand, Arisa!

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.310
What's so great about being a mechanic?

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:20.850
I won't run away.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:24.540
Even if I never catch up to Shipon, I'll never give up on being a pilot!

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:26.910
I'm not running away.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:28.530
And it's no fair for you...

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:32.170
...to vent all your pent-up feelings toward Shipon one-sidedly, Akira!

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:40.120
I'm home. I was given a cake.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.390
Akira, eat it with me...

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.160
Did something happen?

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.620
Oh! No, no, no... That was close...

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.480
Oh, man, I lost.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.260
Heya! It's open!

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:11.700
You're the one who suggested this.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.590
Go on.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.840
Hey, I got a cake.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.490
I was thinking maybe we could all eat it together.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.630
You'll eat some too, right, Shipon?

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.520
I got it from the place where we ordered...

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.330
...the cakes for the graduation party.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.770
It's all right to have little extras like these, right?

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:41.110
Oh, you like cream puffs, right, Shipon?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:41.830
No.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.000
The ones they make there are delicious.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.250
They're even recommended by the sweets master himself, Dai-chan...

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:46.870
Leave me alone.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:51.200
I can't leave you alone. Everyone's worried about you.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.740
Shipon, something happened, didn't it?

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.630
I can't say that I can do anything about it...

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.450
...but it might make you feel better if you talk about it.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.940
Don't they say that all secrets will come out?

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:04.700
That's not it.
 What?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.880
I'm with everyone, but I'm the only one who's different.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.830
I'm different from Kouta, too.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.450
I'm the only one who stands in a different place.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:15.490
It feels like I'm the only one living in a different time.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:20.810
I know the feeling...

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.320
You're supposed to be together, but everyone else is different.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.120
Somehow it feels like you're in your own world...

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.280
...on the other side of the mirror...

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.980
But you are with everyone else, so it's just so hard on you...

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.870
You know everything, don't you, Yayoi?

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:36.450
What?

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:39.170
You are an adult, aren't you, Yayoi?

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.760
You know what I'm worried about and everything else, too, right?

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.720
That's not it, I...

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.730
But I can't be like you, Yayoi!

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.640
I'm a kid!

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:50.590
Shipon!

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.510
You're being pathetic right now, Shipon!

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.970
It's horrible to say that to a friend who's worried about you!

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:57.040
Arisa...

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.440
Stop it. It was my fault from the start...

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.060
Shut up, Akira.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.910
Right now, Shipon is completely in the wrong.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.750
There is what Akira did...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.260
...but first you have to apologize to Milady, Shipon.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.560
Arisa, I don't mind...

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:12.860
Shipon!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.540
You're meddling, Arisa!

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.080
I'm your friend. Of course I'm going to meddle!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.210
Stop it, Arisa!

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.270
I'm the bad one, arbitrarily trying to understand how she feels.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.120
That's not it, Yayoi. I'm the bad one!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:27.580
I can't stand this anymore!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.500
Shipon!

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.340
Stop it!

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.970
Are you her mother or something now?

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:35.330
When your friend is wrong, you should give her advice, right?

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.510
Well, you are her best friend, after all!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.430
Wha...?

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:41.190
Let's just leave her be...

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:45.680
I think it would be best to give her some time to cool off...

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:49.810
And ourselves, too.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.780
What's happening?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:16.910
Who knows?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.180
Rinna, do you know anything?

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.350
Times like this happen between girls.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:25.240
Is that right?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.510
That's right.

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:34.870
Shipon, I...

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:46.460
You're kidding, right?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:47.650
It's true, I tell you.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.330
Are you all right, Fujisawa?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:52.910
Yeah.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:56.440
I'm sorry. I wonder if I'm tired.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:03.800
What's wrong?

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:06.210
Hmm? This and that.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.220
Hmm...?

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.640
Arisa Glennorth.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:13.990
I'd like to talk to you. Do you have time?

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:17.920
So what is it?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:23.390
I thought I should tell you, since you're Miss Katase's best friend.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:24.310
Huh...?

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:30.850
They used the new DLS on the mission that she took part in recently.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.960
With it, you can control everything just by thinking.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.700
Also, you can analyze 100 times the amount of data.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:38.900
Whoa...

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:43.510
But the number of people who are able to use it is limited.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.800
Out of the entire human race...

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.660
...just Otoyama and Miss Katase, only the two of them can.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.570
Out of the entire human race?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.820
Whoa... Shipon and Kouta really are amazing.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:55.890
That's true.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.970
Miss Katase really is amazing.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:02.740
But only when it comes to her skill at controlling a spacecraft.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:06.850
During the mission, Miss Katase was crying in the cockpit.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.380
It sounded like she cried for six hours straight.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.620
For six hours? Why?

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:16.130
Perhaps because she realized the difference in level...

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.430
...between herself and Otoyama.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:21.740
There are things Otoyama can see that Miss Katase cannot.

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:24.260
So because she lost to Kouta?

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.170
That wasn't it. I'm certain of that...

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.620
Maybe she felt like she was being left behind by the person she loves.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.430
She can't be in the same place as the person she loves.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.830
She doesn't understand the person she loves...

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:40.830
Oh...

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.720
A completely starry sky...

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.230
But stars that seem so crowded together...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.590
...actually exist very far apart.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:57.600
Hmm?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.340
People are the same.

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.710
Even if it looks like they're in the same place...

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:03.550
...they're actually far apart.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.890
People are alone, aren't they?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.730
That's why people want to know each other.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:18.710
It's empty...

