00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:28.660
The ups and downs of life... huh?

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:38.140
I'll be able to... get up again, right?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:38.390
Darumaya

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:47.290
It's no use... I can't concentrate at all.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:55.520
Um... is Shipon there?

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:57.080
She hasn't come here.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:58.470
I see...

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:00.520
H-Hey...

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:02.000
Yeah?

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:02.950
I...

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.170
I...?

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:08.090
I'd like you to tell Shipon I'm waiting for her...

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:10.240
...and that I haven't eaten yet, if you see her.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:12.870
Sure...

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:13.910
See you.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:16.510
See you.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:22.270
Miss Katase?

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.360
Nope. Should I call if I see her?

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:28.950
Would you do that? I think she'll be back soon, though.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.340
Okay, see you.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:31.350
Yeah, see you.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.050
Welcome home.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.990
I heard... that you cried for six hours straight...

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.420
Akira was worried, too.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.560
She thought it might be her fault.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.830
I wanted you to talk to me about it.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:58.670
I... I might not understand, but talk to me.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.330
I want to understand you, Shipon!

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.810
There's no way you could understand me!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.750
Arisa, you, Kouta, Yayoi, Akira, everyone...

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.280
None of you are me!

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:10.910
There's no way you could understand!

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:12.990
Just leave me alone!

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:17.670
I can't leave you alone!

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.990
Weren't you working on preparations for the graduation ceremony?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.860
No, I was just wandering aimlessly.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:39.390
Aimlessly?

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:43.670
I thought it might take my mind off things, but it didn't work.

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:45.290
How about you, Akira?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:49.970
I can't... really relax either...

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.690
You'd never understand, Arisa!

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.160
Stop it, Shipon!

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:04.030
Try and talk to me to see if I'd understand or not!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.070
Stop it, Arisa!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.260
I can never be like you, Arisa!

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.630
Or like Kouta or like Yayoi!

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:11.400
That just can't be helped!

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:12.120
Arisa!

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:13.710
Stop it, you two.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.770
After all, you both are good friends!

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.770
Am I the only one who thought we were friends?

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:25.940
I... I'm the only one who's alone!

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:27.420
Shipon!

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.560
It looks like you were going to run out...

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:54.400
What...?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.180
Me too...

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.850
We were all thinking the same thing...

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:16.110
Dummy! Don't cry! Don't cry...

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:49.430
Shima-chan!

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.310
What can I say...

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.310
Good morning, Shipon!

00:20:58.680 --> 00:20:59.370
Morning.

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:05.480
Hey, Shipon, how about we stop by Ashell on the way home from school?

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:05.760
What?

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.280
You know, the shop we talked about yesterday.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:09.470
S-Sure.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:14.440
Oh, man, my usual vending machine was undergoing maintenance.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:16.380
Another one would be fine, right?

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:20.340
What are you talking about? I've got to have this before first bell!

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:26.560
If I don't drink this, then I just can't get started.

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:28.720
It's delicious!

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:36.710
Hey, I wonder if the one that was in the magazine is still available.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.300
The red and green one.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:41.070
Well, it did say that it was popular...

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.820
If it's popular, then they probably made a whole lot.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.520
No problem, no problem!

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.290
Big sister, I really don't understand girls after all.

00:21:55.070 --> 00:22:00.600
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.070 --> 00:22:00.600
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.070 --> 00:22:00.600
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:07.280
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:07.280
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:07.280
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:15.040
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:15.040
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:15.040
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:20.950
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:20.950
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:20.950
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:28.730
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:28.730
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:28.730
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:35.650
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:35.650
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:35.650
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:42.440
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:42.440
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:42.440
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:51.610
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:51.610
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:51.610
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:58.660
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:58.660
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:58.660
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:04.570
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:04.570
And still I looked up

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:04.570
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:06.350
This is Shima.

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:06.980
This is Arisa! 

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:08.340
Thank you for the food!

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:09.270
Stop it! Don't just help yourself to the ice cream...

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:11.320
...in other people's refrigerators!

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:13.000
But there's so much of it here.

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:15.250
We're stocking up! Of course there is!

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:15.860
Why?

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:19.040
Because right after a bath, you eat some ice cream...

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:21.900
...and your teeth get numb, and your temples freeze up...

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:24.360
It's the greatest.

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:25.140
Oh, it's delicious.

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:27.920
Bus gas explosion! 
Dodge...

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:29.890
Why me?

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:31.760
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:32.780
..."Let There Be a Future For You".

